<title>UK: EMAP H1 pre-tax rises 34 percent.</title>
<headline>EMAP H1 pre-tax rises 34 percent.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to September 30</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence, adjusted)    16.0		 vs  12.0</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	    4.3		 vs   3.7</p>
<p> Pretax, pre-excep	  50.6		 vs  37.8</p>
<p> Turnover		    388.3		 vs 334.1</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts' forecasts on pre-tax profits were in a range of 43.5 to 49.0 million stg.  </p>
<p> Operating result	 55.3		   vs 38.9</p>
<p> Exceptional		113.5		  vs 3.9 loss</p>
<p> Interest paid	    6.2		    vs 6.2</p>
<p> Tax			  42.5		   vs 10.2</p>
<p> Net taxed		  121.6		  vs 23.7</p>
<p> Attributable	     119.1		  vs 21.1</p>
<p> Retained		   110.3		  vs 13.5</p>
<p> Pay date		   January 10, 1997</p>
<p>Div registration date  December 3, 1996  Ex-div date		November 25, 1996</p>
